WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.358
The answer to check three:
whether its network is linked

2
00:00:03.358 --> 00:00:06.450
to a DDoS protection plan,
and the portal's spoke isn't.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.425
Scene four.

4
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.711
DDoS protection stops at
layers three and four;

5
00:00:10.711 --> 00:00:13.912
layer seven needs a web
application firewall.

6
00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:16.058
Microsoft Learn is plain about it:

7
00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:20.274
detection mode logs and forwards,
and only prevention mode blocks.

8
00:00:20.274 --> 00:00:23.487
The portal's gateway policy
is still in detection.

9
00:00:23.487 --> 00:00:27.613
Its Front Door policy blocks, but
has no bot protection rule set.

10
00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:31.356
The kit checks every policy on
both services the same way,

11
00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:35.576
and writes the switch to prevention
to a plan, which it never runs.

12
00:00:35.576 --> 00:00:39.820
The application owner runs it,
after reviewing the false positives.
